        "value": "<p>The specimen consists of one gray-white soft tissue mass measuring 2.5 x 1.8 x 1.0 cm. The external surface is smooth. Serial sections reveal a homogenous gray-white cut surface.</p>\n<p><br>MICROSCOPIC DESCRIPTION<br>[Describe the histological findings. Example:]</p>\n<p>Sections show fibrocollagenous tissue infiltrated by nests and cords of malignant epithelial cells with hyperchromatic nuclei, increased nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ratio, and occasional mitotic figures. Focal necrosis is present.</p>\n<p><br>DIAGNOSIS<br><br>[Provide the histopathological diagnosis. Example:]</p>\n<p>- Invasive Ductal Carcinoma &ndash; Grade II (Nottingham grading system)<br>- Lymphovascular invasion: Not seen<br>- Margins: Free of tumor</p>\n<p>------------------------------------------------------------<br>COMMENTS (if any)<br>------------------------------------------------------------<br>[Optional: add clarification, suggestions for IHC, or second opinion details.</p>",
